      "message": "start() is called by tethering main thread so that the socket also be created in tethering main thread. But the socket is used by ra handler thread. In practice, I don\u0027t think the race condition problem will hapeen but in theory using same variable in different without lock is risk.\n\nPer talk offline, I suggest move createSocket() into constructor and make mSocket final. The follow up CL is fine but I think they should be released together.\n\nAlso move closeSocket (at l.410) into ra handler thread.",
